"ap-definition-en" : {"en": "An access point through which an AI agent can be invoked, with its protocol binding and security scheme. It is a specialisation of Data Service, so the endpoint URL, conformance to a standard, access rights and endpoint description are inherited."}, "ap-usageNote-en" : {"en": "An A2A Agent Card describes the agent and all of its interfaces. Link the card once from the AI agent with has native description, and not from each interface.#NOTES#An A2A Agent Card describes the agent and all of its interfaces. Link the card once from the AI agent with has native description, and not from each interface."}, "usage" : {"en": "An A2A Agent Card describes the agent and all of its interfaces. Link the card once from the AI agent with has native description, and not from each interface.#NOTES#An A2A Agent Card describes the agent and all of its interfaces. Link the card once from the AI agent with has native description, and not from each interface."}, "ap-label-en" : {"en": "Agent Interface"}, "definition" : {"en": "An access point through which an AI agent can be invoked, with its protocol binding and security scheme. It is a specialisation of Data Service, so the endpoint URL, conformance to a standard, access rights and endpoint description are inherited."}, "label" : {"en": "Agent Interface"},
