"@type": "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class",
"ap-definition-en" : {"en": "A means by which an AI system informs people that they are interacting with an AI system."}, "ap-usageNote-en" : {"en": "Declared by the provider for AI systems that interact directly with natural persons (AI Act, Article 50(1)). A system can have several disclosures, each with its own channel, wording and timing. Information that is only available in terms of use, URLs or #NOTES#Declared by the provider for AI systems that interact directly with natural persons (AI Act, Article 50(1)). A system can have several disclosures, each with its own channel, wording and timing. Information that is only available in terms of use, URLs or documentation is not a disclosure in this sense. The labelling duties of deployers under Article 50(3) and (4) and the marking of outputs under Article 50(2) are not described by this class."}, "usage" : {"en": "Declared by the provider for AI systems that interact directly with natural persons (AI Act, Article 50(1)). A system can have several disclosures, each with its own channel, wording and timing. Information that is only available in terms of use, URLs or #NOTES#Declared by the provider for AI systems that interact directly with natural persons (AI Act, Article 50(1)). A system can have several disclosures, each with its own channel, wording and timing. Information that is only available in terms of use, URLs or documentation is not a disclosure in this sense. The labelling duties of deployers under Article 50(3) and (4) and the marking of outputs under Article 50(2) are not described by this class."}, "ap-label-en" : {"en": "Disclosure"}, "definition" : {"en": "A means by which an AI system informs people that they are interacting with an AI system."}, "label" : {"en": "Disclosure"},
